  "id": "acceptance-sampling",
  "term": "acceptance sampling",
  "definition": "Acceptance sampling is a method for deciding whether to accept or reject a lot by examining sample data and estimating the probability of acceptance. In the described approach, the decision can depend not only on the current lot’s quality but also on the quality of previous lots.",
